<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Mansur Muhammad II of Hama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1229–1284</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-yahya-hamid-al-din">al-Mansur Muhammad</a> II was the Ayyubid prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hama">Hama</a> from 1244 to 1284. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in 1260 he joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> and fought at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ain-jalut">Ain Jalut</a>, and as a loyal Mamluk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> he kept his principality when the other Ayyubid states disappeared. His descendants included the historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-al-fida">Abu al-Fida</a>.</p></div>
